WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.900
Why code?

2
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.413
Because a review set up by hand drifts.

3
00:00:03.413 --> 00:00:06.177
A reviewer leaves, a
duration is shortened,

4
00:00:06.177 --> 00:00:09.888
auto-apply is switched off for
one cycle and never back on.

5
00:00:09.888 --> 00:00:11.912
And reviews have their own lockout.

6
00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:17.024
The emergency accounts hold Global
Administrator as permanent active assignments.

7
00:00:17.024 --> 00:00:22.129
A review of Global Administrator that
covers active assignments, with remove

8
00:00:22.129 --> 00:00:27.312
access on silence and auto-apply on, removes
them if the reviewers miss one month.

9
00:00:27.312 --> 00:00:30.858
Microsoft Learn's reference
for review settings cautions

10
00:00:30.858 --> 00:00:34.549
that auto-apply with a default
decision can revoke all access.

11
00:00:34.549 --> 00:00:38.768
So rule A R oh six fails a review
that would do that, and rule A R,

12
00:00:38.768 --> 00:00:42.900
E oh eight, reports an emergency
account a reviewer denied.

13
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.788
The apply refuses a plan with any finding.

14
00:00:45.788 --> 00:00:47.865
And the code never deletes a series,

15
00:00:47.865 --> 00:00:52.510
because deleting a definition deletes
its decisions, and those are evidence.
